    "show_share": true,
    "description": "In the last few years, as sophisticated medicines were introduced in the market, disease-causing agents bacteria evolved rapidly to develop resistance. At some point, the pace of evolution outdid the pace of drug development and now scientists are baffled as the lines between treatable and untreatable diseases have blurred.",
